IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 78D to 78K -- Division 3A, reduction of share capital: the creditor's right to object, the position
-- at the end of the objection period, the Court's power, the reduction approved by the Court, the creditor protection, the offences, and the members' liability.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 9502-9881 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
-- "beginning with" counts the day named as day 1 (fork F-P1): the keel's `period: ...` functions are called with the count less one.

§ `Section 78D: the creditor's right to object to the reduction`

-- src:9504 | 78D.—(1) This section applies where a company has passed a
-- src:9505 | special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or
-- src:9506 | 78C.
@ref s 78D(1) (src:9504-9506)
GIVEN `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78D(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where a company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C"; no word says it applies only there, and nothing here covers any other resolution {MR-b}

-- src:9512 | (3) Subsection (2) applies to a creditor of the company who, at the
-- src:9513 | date of the creditor’s application to the Court, is entitled to any debt or
-- src:9514 | claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up
-- src:9515 | of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company.
@ref s 78D(3) (src:9512-9515)
GIVEN `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78D(3) subsection (2) applies to the creditor` MEANS
    IF `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies to a creditor of the company who, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to any debt or claim which ... would be admissible in proof" -- no "only"; a creditor without such a debt or claim is outside the subsection and the text says no more {F-78D1} {MR-b}

-- (2): "Any creditor ... may, at any time during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled." The 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date run from day 0 to day 41 (fork F-P1); an application outside them is outside the period the text fixes (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)).
-- src:9508 | (2) Any creditor of the company to which this subsection applies
-- src:9509 | may, at any time during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution
-- src:9510 | date, apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled.
@ref s 78D(2) (src:9508-9510)
GIVEN `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the date of the creditor's application to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78D(2) the creditor may apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C`) OR (NOT `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) is in a section that "applies where a company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C" and "applies to a creditor of the company who ... is entitled to any debt or claim"; a creditor or company outside those is outside it {F-78D1} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF (`the date of the creditor's application to the Court` AT LEAST `the resolution date`) AND (`the date of the creditor's application to the Court` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, at any time during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, apply to the Court" -- an application before the resolution date or after the 41st day after it is outside the period the text fixes {F-78D2} {MR-b} {MR-a}

DECLARE `s 78D act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78D(4)(a) serve the application on the company`
    `s 78D(4)(b) give to the Registrar notice of the application`

-- (4)(a) and (b) say "as soon as possible", which is no day: the rules have no deadline and cannot reach BREACH (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:9517 | (4) When an application is made under subsection (2) —
-- src:9519 | (a) the creditor must as soon as possible serve the application
-- src:9520 | on the company; and
@ref s 78D(4)(a) (src:9517-9520)
GIVEN `the name of the creditor` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78D act`
`s 78D(4)(a) the creditor must as soon as possible serve the application on the company` MEANS
    PARTY Creditor `the name of the creditor`
    MUST `s 78D(4)(a) serve the application on the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:9517 | (4) When an application is made under subsection (2) —
-- src:9522 | (b) the company must as soon as possible give to the Registrar
-- src:9523 | notice of the application.
@ref s 78D(4)(b) (src:9517-9523)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78D act`
`s 78D(4)(b) the company must as soon as possible give to the Registrar notice of the application` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78D(4)(b) give to the Registrar notice of the application`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 78E: the position at the end of the period for creditor objections`

-- (1)(d), (2): "after the end of 6 weeks, and before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution date": from day 42 to day 55, both counted (fork F-78E1).
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9547 | (d) the following documents after the end of 6 weeks, and
-- src:9548 | before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution
-- src:9549 | date:
@ref s 78E(1)(d) (src:9547-9549)
GIVEN `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78E(1)(d) the documents are lodged after the end of 6 weeks and before the end of 8 weeks beginning with the resolution date` MEANS
        `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days
    AND `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 55 Days

-- (1): a private company, no application. The lead-in is a "Where": when it is not met the subsection does not apply, which the periods ruling of 2026-11-05 (item (b)) answers FALSE (fork F-78E2).
-- "for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the company must lodge": a condition of taking effect, not a duty with its own penalty (fork F-78E3); an unmet requirement is the text's no.
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9530 | 78E.—(1) Where —
-- src:9532 | (a) a private company passes a special resolution for reducing
-- src:9533 | its share capital and meets the requirements under
-- src:9534 | section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under
-- src:9535 | section 78B(3) (if applicable); and
-- src:9537 | (b) no application for cancellation of the resolution has been
-- src:9538 | made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning
-- src:9539 | with the resolution date,
-- src:9541 | for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the company must
-- src:9542 | lodge with the Registrar —
-- src:9544 | (c) a copy of the resolution in accordance with section 186;
-- src:9545 | and
-- src:9547 | (d) the following documents after the end of 6 weeks, and
-- src:9548 | before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution
-- src:9549 | date:
-- src:9551 | (i) a copy of the solvency statement under
-- src:9552 | section 78B(3) (if applicable);
-- src:9554 | (ii) a statement made by the directors confirming that the
-- src:9555 | requirements under section 78B(1)(c) and the
-- src:9556 | solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if
-- src:9557 | applicable) have been complied with, and that no
-- src:9558 | application for cancellation of the resolution has
-- src:9559 | been made;
-- src:9561 | (iii) a notice containing the reduction information.
@ref s 78E(1) (src:9530-9561)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the requirements under section 78B(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the resolution in accordance with section 186` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the solvency statement under section 78B(3) (if applicable)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable) have been complied with, and that no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78E(1) the private company has lodged what the subsection requires for the reduction of share capital to take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR (NOT `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital`) OR (NOT `the company meets the requirements under section 78B(1)(c)`) OR (NOT `the company meets the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable)`) OR `an application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where — (a) a private company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital and meets the requirements ...; and (b) no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" -- the case the subsection describes does not arise {F-78E2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the resolution in accordance with section 186`
            AND (`s 78E(1)(d) the documents are lodged after the end of 6 weeks and before the end of 8 weeks beginning with the resolution date` `the resolution date` `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar`)
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the solvency statement under section 78B(3) (if applicable)`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable) have been complied with, and that no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; the requirement is unmet): "for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the company must lodge with the Registrar — (c) a copy of the resolution in accordance with section 186; and (d) the following documents after the end of 6 weeks, and before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution date" {F-78E1} {F-78E3} {MR-a}

-- (2): a public company, no application: the directors' statement and the notice, in the same window.
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9565 | (2) Where —
-- src:9567 | (a) a public company passes a special resolution for reducing
-- src:9568 | its share capital and meets the requirements under
-- src:9569 | section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements (if
-- src:9570 | applicable) under section 78C(3); and
-- src:9572 | (b) no application for cancellation of the resolution has been
-- src:9573 | made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning
-- src:9574 | with the resolution date,
-- src:9579 | for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the company must
-- src:9580 | lodge with the Registrar the following documents after the end of
-- src:9581 | 6 weeks, and before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution
-- src:9582 | date:
-- src:9584 | (c) a statement made by the directors confirming that the
-- src:9585 | requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency
-- src:9586 | requirements under section 78C(3) (if applicable) have
-- src:9587 | been complied with, and that no application for
-- src:9588 | cancellation of the resolution has been made;
-- src:9590 | (d) a notice containing the reduction information. [36/2014]
@ref s 78E(2) (src:9565-9590)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements (if applicable) under section 78C(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78C(3) (if applicable) have been complied with, and that no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78E(2) the public company has lodged what the subsection requires for the reduction of share capital to take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital`) OR (NOT `the company meets the requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements (if applicable) under section 78C(3)`) OR `an application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where — (a) a public company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital and meets the requirements ...; and (b) no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" -- the case the subsection describes does not arise {F-78E2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    (`s 78E(1)(d) the documents are lodged after the end of 6 weeks and before the end of 8 weeks beginning with the resolution date` `the resolution date` `the date the documents were lodged with the Registrar`)
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78C(3) (if applicable) have been complied with, and that no application for cancellation of the resolution has been made`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; the requirement is unmet): "for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the company must lodge with the Registrar the following documents after the end of 6 weeks, and before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution date" {F-78E1} {F-78E3} {MR-a}

-- (3): a private company, with applications made. (e): "within 15 days beginning with the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end": day 0 to day 14 (fork F-P1).
-- src:9591 | (3) Where —
-- src:9593 | (a) a private company passes a special resolution for reducing
-- src:9594 | its share capital and meets the requirements under
-- src:9595 | section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under
-- src:9596 | section 78B(3) (if applicable); but
-- src:9598 | (b) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, one
-- src:9599 | or more applications for cancellation of the resolution are
-- src:9600 | made under section 78D(2),
-- src:9602 | for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the following
-- src:9603 | conditions must be satisfied:
-- src:9605 | (c) the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b)
-- src:9606 | (notification to Registrar) in relation to all such
-- src:9607 | applications;
-- src:9609 | (d) the proceedings in relation to each such application have
-- src:9610 | been brought to an end —
-- src:9612 | (i) by the dismissal of the application under section 78F;
-- src:9613 | or
-- src:9615 | (ii) without determination (for example, because the
-- src:9616 | application has been withdrawn);
-- src:9618 | (e) the company has, within 15 days beginning with the date
-- src:9619 | on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end
-- src:9620 | in accordance with paragraph (d), lodged with the
-- src:9621 | Registrar —
-- src:9626 | (i) a statement made by the directors confirming that the
-- src:9627 | requirements under section 78B(1)(c), the solvency
-- src:9628 | requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable)
-- src:9629 | and section 78D(4)(b) have been complied with, and
-- src:9630 | that the proceedings in relation to each such
-- src:9631 | application have been brought to an end by the
-- src:9632 | dismissal of the application or without
-- src:9633 | determination;
-- src:9635 | (ii) in relation to each such application which has been
-- src:9636 | dismissed by the Court, a copy of the order of the
-- src:9637 | Court dismissing the application; and
-- src:9639 | (iii) a notice containing the reduction information.
@ref s 78E(3) (src:9591-9639)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the requirements under section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more applications for cancellation of the resolution have been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b) (notification to Registrar) in relation to all such applications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application under section 78F or without determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78B(1)(c), the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable) and section 78D(4)(b) have been complied with, and that the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application or without determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar, in relation to each such application which has been dismissed by the Court, a copy of the order of the Court dismissing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78E(3) the private company has satisfied the conditions for the reduction of share capital to take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR (NOT `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital`) OR (NOT `the company meets the requirements under section 78B(1)(c) and the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable)`) OR (NOT `one or more applications for cancellation of the resolution have been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where — (a) a private company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital and meets the requirements ...; but (b) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, one or more applications for cancellation of the resolution are made under section 78D(2)" -- the case the subsection describes does not arise {F-78E2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b) (notification to Registrar) in relation to all such applications`
            AND `the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application under section 78F or without determination`
            AND (`the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end`)
            AND (`the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end` 14 Days)
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78B(1)(c), the solvency requirements under section 78B(3) (if applicable) and section 78D(4)(b) have been complied with, and that the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application or without determination`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar, in relation to each such application which has been dismissed by the Court, a copy of the order of the Court dismissing the application`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; a condition is unmet): "for the reduction of share capital to take effect, the following conditions must be satisfied: (c) the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b) ...; (d) the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end ...; (e) the company has, within 15 days beginning with the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end ..., lodged with the Registrar" {F-78E3} {F-78E4} {MR-a}

-- (4): a public company, with applications made.
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
