      `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78C(1)(c), the solvency requirements under section 78C(3) (if applicable) and section 78D(4) have been complied with, and that the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application or without determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar, in relation to each such application which has been dismissed by the Court, a copy of the order of the Court dismissing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78E(4) the public company has satisfied the conditions for the reduction of capital to take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital`) OR (NOT `the company meets the requirements under section 78C(1)(c) and the solvency requirements (if applicable) under section 78C(3)`) OR (NOT `one or more applications for cancellation of the resolution have been made under section 78D(2) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where — (a) a public company passes a special resolution for reducing its share capital and meets the requirements ...; but (b) during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, one or more applications for cancellation of the resolution are made under section 78D(2)" -- the case the subsection describes does not arise {F-78E2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b) (notification to Registrar) in relation to all such applications`
            AND `the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application under section 78F or without determination`
            AND (`the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end`)
            AND (`the date the documents in paragraph (e) were lodged with the Registrar` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end` 14 Days)
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a statement made by the directors confirming that the requirements under section 78C(1)(c), the solvency requirements under section 78C(3) (if applicable) and section 78D(4) have been complied with, and that the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end by the dismissal of the application or without determination`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar, in relation to each such application which has been dismissed by the Court, a copy of the order of the Court dismissing the application`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; a condition is unmet): "for the reduction of capital to take effect, the following conditions must be satisfied: (c) the company has complied with section 78D(4)(b) ...; (d) the proceedings in relation to each such application have been brought to an end ...; (e) the company has, within 15 days beginning with the date on which the last such proceedings were brought to an end ..., lodged with the Registrar" {F-78E3} {F-78E4} {MR-a}

-- (5): "The resolution ... and the reduction of the share capital, take effect when the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her in the appropriate register."
-- src:9696 | (5) The resolution in a case referred to in subsection (1), (2), (3) or
-- src:9697 | (4), and the reduction of the share capital, take effect when the
-- src:9698 | Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her in the
-- src:9699 | appropriate register.
@ref s 78E(5) (src:9696-9699)
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4) and the lodgement it requires has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78E(5) the resolution and the reduction of the share capital take effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the case is one referred to in subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4) and the lodgement it requires has been made`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The resolution in a case referred to in subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4), and the reduction of the share capital, take effect when the Registrar has recorded the information"; a case outside those four is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her in the appropriate register`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "take effect when the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her in the appropriate register" -- before then the resolution and the reduction have not taken effect (a "when" gate read as the only time, fork F-78E5) {F-78E5} {MR-a}

§ `Section 78F: the Court's power where a creditor objects`

-- (1): the section governs how an application by a creditor under s 78D is determined; the Court is the actor and the creditor is the bearer.
-- src:9703 | 78F.—(1) An application by a creditor under section 78D is to be
-- src:9704 | determined by the Court in accordance with this section.
@ref s 78F(1) (src:9703-9704)
GIVEN `the application is an application by a creditor under section 78D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(1) the application is to be determined by the Court in accordance with section 78F` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application by a creditor under section 78D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application by a creditor under section 78D is to be determined by the Court in accordance with this section"; an application of another kind is outside it {MR-b}

-- (2) and (3): the Court must cancel if all the listed conditions hold; "Otherwise, the Court is to dismiss the application".
-- src:9706 | (2) The Court must make an order cancelling the resolution if, at the
-- src:9707 | time the application is considered, the resolution has not been
-- src:9708 | cancelled previously, any debt or claim on which the application was
-- src:9709 | based is outstanding and the Court is satisfied that —
-- src:9711 | (a) the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant
-- src:9712 | does not have other adequate safeguards for it; and
-- src:9714 | (b) it is not the case that security or other safeguards are
-- src:9715 | unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would
-- src:9716 | have after the reduction.
@ref s 78F(2) (src:9706-9716)
GIVEN `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(2) the Court must make an order cancelling the resolution` MEANS
    IF    `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously`
      AND `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding`
      AND `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it`
      AND (NOT `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) Otherwise, the Court is to dismiss the application" -- the conditions of subsection (2) are not all met, so the Court does not cancel and is to dismiss {F-78F1} {MR-a}

-- src:9718 | (3) Otherwise, the Court is to dismiss the application.
@ref s 78F(3) (src:9718-9718)
GIVEN `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(3) the Court is to dismiss the application` MEANS
    IF (`s 78F(2) the Court must make an order cancelling the resolution` `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) Otherwise, the Court is to dismiss the application" -- the conditions of subsection (2) are all met, so the case is not "otherwise" {F-78F1} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4): "the company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made": day 0 to day 14 (fork F-P1). The lead-in is a "Where": unmet, it is FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)).
-- src:9723 | (4) Where the Court makes an order under subsection (2), the
-- src:9724 | company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days
-- src:9725 | beginning with the date the order is made.
@ref s 78F(4) (src:9723-9725)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the company has sent notice of the order to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company sent notice of the order to the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(4) the company has contravened subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court has made an order under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where the Court makes an order under subsection (2), the company must send notice of the order" -- no order, so no duty {F-78F4} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the company has sent notice of the order to the Registrar`
            AND (`the date the company sent notice of the order to the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date the order is made`)
            AND (`the date the company sent notice of the order to the Registrar` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order is made` 14 Days)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "the company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made" -- the duty is met, so no contravention {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:9727 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (4), every officer of the
-- src:9728 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78F(5) (src:9727-9728)
GIVEN `the company contravenes subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(5) the officer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes subsection (4)` AND `the person is an officer of the company` AND `the officer is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-78F2): "If a company contravenes subsection (4), every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence {F-78F2} {MR-a}

-- src:9730 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a debt is outstanding if it has not
-- src:9731 | been discharged, and a claim is outstanding if it has not been
-- src:9732 | terminated.
@ref s 78F(6) (src:9730-9732)
GIVEN `the debt has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(6) the debt is outstanding` MEANS
    IF `the debt has been discharged`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "a debt is outstanding if it has not been discharged" -- the "if" is unmet (read as the whole of the meaning, fork F-78F3) {F-78F3} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9730 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a debt is outstanding if it has not
-- src:9731 | been discharged, and a claim is outstanding if it has not been
-- src:9732 | terminated.
@ref s 78F(6) (src:9730-9732)
GIVEN `the claim has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78F(6) the claim is outstanding` MEANS
    IF `the claim has been terminated`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "a claim is outstanding if it has not been terminated" -- the "if" is unmet (read as the whole of the meaning, fork F-78F3) {F-78F3} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 78F act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78F(4) send notice of the order to the Registrar`

-- Day 0 is the date the order is made; "within 15 days beginning with" it ends on day 14.
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9723 | (4) Where the Court makes an order under subsection (2), the
-- src:9724 | company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days
-- src:9725 | beginning with the date the order is made.
@ref s 78F(4) (src:9723-9725)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78F act`
`s 78F(4) the company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78F(4) send notice of the order to the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order was made"

§ `Section 78G: reduction by special resolution subject to Court approval`

-- src:9736 | 78G.—(1) A company limited by shares may, as an alternative to
-- src:9737 | reducing its share capital under section 78B or 78C, reduce it in any
-- src:9738 | way by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under
-- src:9739 | section 78I, but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital do
-- src:9740 | not take effect until —
-- src:9742 | (a) that order has been made;
-- src:9744 | (b) the company has complied with section 78I(3) (lodgment
-- src:9745 | of information with Registrar); and
-- src:9747 | (c) the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him
-- src:9748 | or her under section 78I(3) in the appropriate register.
@ref s 78G(1) (src:9736-9748)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the reduction is by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under section 78I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78G(1) the company limited by shares may reduce its share capital in any way by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court` MEANS
    IF (`s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the reduction is by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under section 78I`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, as an alternative to reducing its share capital under section 78B or 78C, reduce it in any way by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under section 78I" -- a grant named "may" whose gate is not met, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {F-78G1} {MR-b}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company limited by shares may"; another company is outside it {MR-b}

-- "but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital do not take effect until — (a) that order has been made; (b) the company has complied with section 78I(3); and (c) the Registrar has recorded the information". An "until" bar (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d)): TRUE before all three, FALSE after.
-- src:9736 | 78G.—(1) A company limited by shares may, as an alternative to
-- src:9737 | reducing its share capital under section 78B or 78C, reduce it in any
-- src:9738 | way by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under
-- src:9739 | section 78I, but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital do
-- src:9740 | not take effect until —
-- src:9742 | (a) that order has been made;
-- src:9744 | (b) the company has complied with section 78I(3) (lodgment
-- src:9745 | of information with Registrar); and
-- src:9747 | (c) the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him
-- src:9748 | or her under section 78I(3) in the appropriate register.
@ref s 78G(1) (src:9736-9748)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has complied with section 78I(3) (lodgment of information with Registrar)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her under section 78I(3) in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78G(1) the resolution and the reduction of the share capital cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF (`s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the order has been made` AND `the company has complied with section 78I(3) (lodgment of information with Registrar)` AND `the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him or her under section 78I(3) in the appropriate register`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not take effect until — (a) that order has been made; (b) the company has complied with section 78I(3) ...; and (c) the Registrar has recorded the information" -- all three are done, so the bar is lifted {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company limited by shares may ... reduce it ... but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital do not take effect until"; another company is outside it {F-78G1} {MR-b}

§ `Section 78H: creditor protection`

-- (1): "This section applies if a company makes an application under section 78G(1) and the proposed reduction ... involves either (a) a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital; or (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital, and also applies if the Court so directs in any other case".
-- src:9754 | 78H.—(1) This section applies if a company makes an application
-- src:9755 | under section 78G(1) and the proposed reduction of share capital
-- src:9756 | involves either —
-- src:9758 | (a) a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital; or
-- src:9760 | (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid‑up share capital,
-- src:9762 | and also applies if the Court so directs in any other case where a
-- src:9763 | company makes an application under that section.
@ref s 78H(1) (src:9754-9763)
GIVEN `the company makes an application under section 78G(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court so directs in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF    `the company makes an application under section 78G(1)`
      AND (`the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` OR `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` OR `the Court so directs in the case`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies if a company makes an application under section 78G(1) and the proposed reduction of share capital involves either ... and also applies if the Court so directs in any other case where a company makes an application under that section" -- no "only if" {F-78H1} {MR-b}

-- src:9765 | (2) Upon the application to the Court, the Court is to settle a list of
-- src:9766 | qualifying creditors.
@ref s 78H(2) (src:9765-9766)
GIVEN `section 78H applies to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(2) the Court is to settle a list of qualifying creditors` MEANS
    IF `section 78H applies to the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Upon the application to the Court, the Court is to settle a list of qualifying creditors" -- in a section that applies only as subsection (1) says; where it does not apply the text says nothing {F-78H1} {MR-b}

-- (3): "the Court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the case it thinks it appropriate to do so, direct that any class or classes of creditors are not qualifying creditors."
-- src:9771 | (3) If the proposed reduction of share capital involves either —
-- src:9773 | (a) a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital; or
-- src:9775 | (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid‑up share capital,
-- src:9777 | the Court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the
-- src:9778 | case it thinks it appropriate to do so, direct that any class or classes of
-- src:9779 | creditors are not qualifying creditors.
@ref s 78H(3) (src:9771-9779)
GIVEN `the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks it appropriate to do so, having regard to any special circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(3) the Court may direct that a class or classes of creditors are not qualifying creditors` MEANS
    IF    (`the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` OR `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital`)
      AND `the Court thinks it appropriate to do so, having regard to any special circumstances of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the proposed reduction of share capital involves either ... the Court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the case it thinks it appropriate to do so, direct" -- a grant named "may" whose "if" gates are not met, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {F-78H2} {MR-b}

DECLARE `s 78H act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78H(4)(a) ascertain the names of qualifying creditors and the nature and amount of their debts or claims`
    `s 78H(5) conceal intentionally the name of a qualifying creditor, misrepresent intentionally the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor, or aid, abet or be privy to such concealment or misrepresentation`

-- (4)(a) names no day by which the Court must act: no deadline, no breach path (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:9781 | (4) For the purpose of settling the list of qualifying creditors, the
-- src:9782 | Court —
-- src:9784 | (a) must ascertain, as far as possible without requiring an
-- src:9785 | application from any creditor, the names of qualifying
-- src:9786 | creditors and the nature and amount of their debts or
-- src:9787 | claims; and
@ref s 78H(4)(a) (src:9781-9787)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78H act`
`s 78H(4)(a) the Court must ascertain the names of qualifying creditors and the nature and amount of their debts or claims` MEANS
    PARTY Court
    MUST `s 78H(4)(a) ascertain the names of qualifying creditors and the nature and amount of their debts or claims`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:9781 | (4) For the purpose of settling the list of qualifying creditors, the
-- src:9782 | Court —
-- src:9789 | (b) may publish notices fixing a day or days within which
-- src:9790 | creditors not included in the list are to claim to be so
-- src:9791 | included or are to be excluded from the list.
@ref s 78H(4)(b) (src:9781-9791)
GIVEN `the notice fixes a day or days within which creditors not included in the list are to claim to be so included or are to be excluded from the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(4)(b) the Court may publish notices` MEANS
    IF `the notice fixes a day or days within which creditors not included in the list are to claim to be so included or are to be excluded from the list`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court ... may publish notices fixing a day or days within which creditors not included in the list are to claim to be so included or are to be excluded from the list" -- a permission; a notice of another kind is not mentioned, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {MR-b}

-- (5): the offence: "(a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor; (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor; or (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation ... a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years."
-- The text gives a fine "or" imprisonment (no "or to both"), so both is FALSE (fork F-78H3).
DECLARE `s 78H(5) penalty` HAS
    `s 78H(5) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 78H(5) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `s 78H(5) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9793 | (5) Any officer of the company who —
-- src:9795 | (a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor;
-- src:9797 | (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the
-- src:9798 | debt or claim of any creditor; or
-- src:9800 | (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or
-- src:9801 | misrepresentation,
-- src:9803 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:9804 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:9805 | 3 years.
@ref s 78H(5) (src:9793-9805)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an officer of the company`
      AND (`the officer intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor` OR `the officer intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor` OR `the officer aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-78H3): "Any officer of the company who — (a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor; (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor; or (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation, shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts {F-78H3} {MR-a}

-- src:9793 | (5) Any officer of the company who —
-- src:9795 | (a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor;
-- src:9797 | (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the
-- src:9798 | debt or claim of any creditor; or
-- src:9800 | (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or
-- src:9801 | misrepresentation,
-- src:9803 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:9804 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:9805 | 3 years.
@ref s 78H(5) (src:9793-9805)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 78H(5) penalty`
`s 78H(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF (`s 78H(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is an officer of the company` `the officer intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor` `the officer intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of any creditor` `the officer aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or misrepresentation`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 78H(5) penalty` OF 15000, 3, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the officer it makes guilty; the fine and the imprisonment are alternatives ("or"), so the court may not impose both under it (fork F-78H3) {F-78H3}

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04: where the text names the bearer, SHANT is derived). The bearer is "any officer of the company".
-- src:9793 | (5) Any officer of the company who —
-- src:9795 | (a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor;
-- src:9797 | (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the
-- src:9798 | debt or claim of any creditor; or
-- src:9800 | (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or
-- src:9801 | misrepresentation,
-- src:9803 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:9804 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:9805 | 3 years.
@ref s 78H(5) (src:9793-9805)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78H act`
`s 78H(5) an officer must not conceal or misrepresent the debts or claims of creditors, or aid or abet it` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 78H(5) conceal intentionally the name of a qualifying creditor, misrepresent intentionally the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor, or aid, abet or be privy to such concealment or misrepresentation`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (6): "“qualifying creditor” means a creditor of the company who, at a date fixed by the Court, is entitled to any debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company", "subject to subsection (3)".
-- src:9807 | (6) In this section and section 78I but subject to subsection (3),
-- src:9808 | “qualifying creditor” means a creditor of the company who, at a date
-- src:9809 | fixed by the Court, is entitled to any debt or claim which, if that date
-- src:9810 | were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be
-- src:9811 | admissible in proof against the company.
@ref s 78H(6) (src:9807-9811)
GIVEN `the creditor, at a date fixed by the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed under subsection (3) that the class of creditors to which the creditor belongs are not qualifying creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78H(6) "qualifying creditor" the creditor is a qualifying creditor` MEANS
    IF `the Court has directed under subsection (3) that the class of creditors to which the creditor belongs are not qualifying creditors`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section and section 78I but subject to subsection (3), “qualifying creditor” means" -- the Court has excluded the class under subsection (3)
    ELSE (IF `the creditor, at a date fixed by the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying creditor” means a creditor of the company who, at a date fixed by the Court, is entitled to any debt or claim which ... would be admissible in proof against the company" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 78I: the Court's order approving the reduction`

-- (2): a bar over the creditors on the Court's list. One record per qualifying creditor; the bar looks at each creditor who is on the list and whose claim or debt is live.
DECLARE `s 78I(2) qualifying creditor` HAS
    `s 78I(2)(a) the creditor is included in the Court's list of qualifying creditors under section 78H` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 78I(2)(b) the creditor's claim has not been terminated or the creditor's debt has not been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 78I(2)(c) the Court is satisfied that the qualifying creditor has consented to the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 78I(2)(d) the Court is satisfied that the qualifying creditor's debt or claim has been secured or the qualifying creditor has other adequate safeguards for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 78I(2)(e) the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets the company would have after the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9824 | (2) If, at the time the Court considers the application, there is a
-- src:9825 | qualifying creditor within the meaning of section 78H —
-- src:9827 | (a) who is included in the Court’s list of qualifying creditors
-- src:9828 | under that section; and
-- src:9830 | (b) whose claim has not been terminated or whose debt has not
-- src:9831 | been discharged,
-- src:9833 | the Court must not make an order approving the reduction unless
-- src:9834 | satisfied, as respects each qualifying creditor, that —
-- src:9836 | (c) the qualifying creditor has consented to the reduction;
-- src:9838 | (d) the qualifying creditor’s debt or claim has been secured or
-- src:9839 | the qualifying creditor has other adequate safeguards for it;
-- src:9840 | or
-- src:9842 | (e) security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the
-- src:9843 | assets the company would have after the reduction.
@ref s 78I(2) (src:9824-9843)
GIVEN creditor IS A `s 78I(2) qualifying creditor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78I(2) the creditor stands in the way of an order approving the reduction` MEANS
        creditor's `s 78I(2)(a) the creditor is included in the Court's list of qualifying creditors under section 78H`
    AND creditor's `s 78I(2)(b) the creditor's claim has not been terminated or the creditor's debt has not been discharged`
    AND (NOT (   creditor's `s 78I(2)(c) the Court is satisfied that the qualifying creditor has consented to the reduction`
              OR creditor's `s 78I(2)(d) the Court is satisfied that the qualifying creditor's debt or claim has been secured or the qualifying creditor has other adequate safeguards for it`
              OR creditor's `s 78I(2)(e) the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets the company would have after the reduction`))

-- src:9824 | (2) If, at the time the Court considers the application, there is a
-- src:9825 | qualifying creditor within the meaning of section 78H —
-- src:9827 | (a) who is included in the Court’s list of qualifying creditors
-- src:9828 | under that section; and
-- src:9830 | (b) whose claim has not been terminated or whose debt has not
-- src:9831 | been discharged,
-- src:9833 | the Court must not make an order approving the reduction unless
-- src:9834 | satisfied, as respects each qualifying creditor, that —
-- src:9836 | (c) the qualifying creditor has consented to the reduction;
-- src:9838 | (d) the qualifying creditor’s debt or claim has been secured or
-- src:9839 | the qualifying creditor has other adequate safeguards for it;
-- src:9840 | or
-- src:9842 | (e) security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the
-- src:9843 | assets the company would have after the reduction.
@ref s 78I(2) (src:9824-9843)
GIVEN creditors IS A LIST OF `s 78I(2) qualifying creditor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78I(2) the Court must not make an order approving the reduction` MEANS
    IF any `s 78I(2) the creditor stands in the way of an order approving the reduction` creditors
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court must not make an order approving the reduction unless satisfied, as respects each qualifying creditor, that — (c) ...; (d) ...; or (e) ..." -- there is no creditor on the list with a live claim or debt who fails all three, so the "unless" is met or the "If" gate is not (a bar keeps FALSE, the grant rule of 2026-11-12) {F-78I1} {MR-a}

-- (1): "the Court may, subject to subsection (2), make an order approving the reduction in share capital unconditionally or on such terms and conditions as it thinks fit."
-- src:9815 | 78I.—(1) On an application by a company under section 78G(1),
-- src:9816 | the Court may, subject to subsection (2), make an order approving the
-- src:9821 | reduction in share capital unconditionally or on such terms and
-- src:9822 | conditions as it thinks fit.
@ref s 78I(1) (src:9815-9822)
GIVEN `the company applies under section 78G(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      creditors IS A LIST OF `s 78I(2) qualifying creditor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78I(1) the Court may make an order approving the reduction in share capital` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company applies under section 78G(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an application by a company under section 78G(1), the Court may"; without such an application the subsection says nothing {F-78I3} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF (`s 78I(2) the Court must not make an order approving the reduction` creditors) EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a bar overrides the grant): "the Court may, subject to subsection (2)" and subsection (2) says the Court "must not make an order approving the reduction unless satisfied" {F-78I1} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (3): "the company must (for the reduction to take effect) lodge with the Registrar — (a) a copy of the order; and (b) a notice containing the reduction information, within 90 days beginning with the date the order is made, or within such longer period as the Registrar may ... allow."
-- 90 days beginning with the date the order is made end on day 89 (fork F-P1). The longer period the Registrar allows is taken as a last day the Registrar names (fork F-78I2). A condition of taking effect, not a duty with its own penalty (fork F-78E3).
-- src:9845 | (3) Where an order is made under this section approving a
-- src:9846 | company’s reduction in share capital, the company must (for the
-- src:9847 | reduction to take effect) lodge with the Registrar —
-- src:9849 | (a) a copy of the order; and
-- src:9851 | (b) a notice containing the reduction information,
-- src:9853 | within 90 days beginning with the date the order is made, or within
-- src:9854 | such longer period as the Registrar may, on the application of the
-- src:9855 | company and on receiving the prescribed fee, allow.
@ref s 78I(3) (src:9845-9855)
GIVEN `the date the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78I(3) the last day for the company to lodge the copy of the order and the notice` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee`
    THEN (IF `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order is made` 89 Days
          THEN `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed`
          ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order is made` 89 Days)
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order is made` 89 Days

-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9845 | (3) Where an order is made under this section approving a
-- src:9846 | company’s reduction in share capital, the company must (for the
-- src:9847 | reduction to take effect) lodge with the Registrar —
-- src:9849 | (a) a copy of the order; and
-- src:9851 | (b) a notice containing the reduction information,
-- src:9853 | within 90 days beginning with the date the order is made, or within
-- src:9854 | such longer period as the Registrar may, on the application of the
-- src:9855 | company and on receiving the prescribed fee, allow.
@ref s 78I(3) (src:9845-9855)
GIVEN `an order is made under section 78I approving a company's reduction in share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company lodged the copy of the order and the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78I(3) the company has lodged the copy of the order and the notice in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `an order is made under section 78I approving a company's reduction in share capital`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where an order is made under this section approving a company's reduction in share capital, the company must ... lodge" -- no order, so no requirement {F-78I2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of the order`
            AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a notice containing the reduction information`
            AND (`the date the company lodged the copy of the order and the notice` AT LEAST `the date the order is made`)
            AND (`the date the company lodged the copy of the order and the notice` AT MOST `s 78I(3) the last day for the company to lodge the copy of the order and the notice` `the date the order is made` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; the requirement is unmet): "the company must (for the reduction to take effect) lodge with the Registrar — (a) a copy of the order; and (b) a notice containing the reduction information, within 90 days beginning with the date the order is made, or within such longer period as the Registrar may, on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee, allow" {F-78I2} {F-78E3} {MR-a}

§ `Section 78J: groundless or false statements`

DECLARE `s 78J act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78J make a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) which is false and which the director does not believe to be true`

-- No penalty is stated in this section, so none is encoded (NOTES.md, "Seams").
-- src:9859 | 78J. A director making a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii),
-- src:9860 | (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) shall be guilty of an offence if the
-- src:9861 | statement —
-- src:9863 | (a) is false; and
-- src:9865 | (b) is not believed by the director to be true.
@ref s 78J (src:9859-9865)
GIVEN `the person is a director who made a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is not believed by the director to be true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78J the director is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director who made a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i)` AND `the statement is false` AND `the statement is not believed by the director to be true`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the section's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-78J1): "A director making a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) shall be guilty of an offence if the statement — (a) is false; and (b) is not believed by the director to be true" -- an element is unmet, so this section makes the director guilty of nothing on these facts {F-78J1} {MR-a}

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04). The bearer is "a director making a statement".
-- src:9859 | 78J. A director making a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii),
-- src:9860 | (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) shall be guilty of an offence if the
-- src:9861 | statement —
-- src:9863 | (a) is false; and
-- src:9865 | (b) is not believed by the director to be true.
@ref s 78J (src:9859-9865)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78J act`
`s 78J a director must not make a false statement which the director does not believe to be true` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 78J make a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) which is false and which the director does not believe to be true`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 78K: liability of members on reduced shares`

-- "Where a company's share capital is reduced under any provision of this Division, a member of the company (past or present) is not liable in respect of the issue price of any share to any call or contribution greater in amount than the difference (if any) between — (a) the issue price of the share; and (b) the aggregate of the amount paid up on the share (if any) and the amount reduced on the share."
-- src:9872 | 78K. Where a company’s share capital is reduced under any
-- src:9873 | provision of this Division, a member of the company (past or present)
-- src:9874 | is not liable in respect of the issue price of any share to any call or
-- src:9875 | contribution greater in amount than the difference (if any) between —
-- src:9877 | (a) the issue price of the share; and
-- src:9879 | (b) the aggregate of the amount paid up on the share (if any)
-- src:9880 | and the amount reduced on the share.
@ref s 78K (src:9872-9880)
GIVEN `the company's share capital is reduced under a provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue price of the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid up on the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount reduced on the share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78K the greatest call or contribution a member is liable to in respect of the issue price of the share` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company's share capital is reduced under a provision of this Division`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company's share capital is reduced under any provision of this Division"; another reduction is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the issue price of the share` MINUS (`the amount paid up on the share` PLUS `the amount reduced on the share`) GREATER THAN 0
          THEN JUST (`the issue price of the share` MINUS (`the amount paid up on the share` PLUS `the amount reduced on the share`))
          ELSE JUST 0)   -- the "(if any)": where there is no difference, the greatest call is nothing {F-78K1}

-- src:9872 | 78K. Where a company’s share capital is reduced under any
-- src:9873 | provision of this Division, a member of the company (past or present)
-- src:9874 | is not liable in respect of the issue price of any share to any call or
-- src:9875 | contribution greater in amount than the difference (if any) between —
-- src:9877 | (a) the issue price of the share; and
-- src:9879 | (b) the aggregate of the amount paid up on the share (if any)
-- src:9880 | and the amount reduced on the share.
@ref s 78K (src:9872-9880)
GIVEN `the company's share capital is reduced under a provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue price of the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid up on the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount reduced on the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the call or contribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78K the member is liable to the call or contribution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company's share capital is reduced under a provision of this Division`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company's share capital is reduced under any provision of this Division"; another reduction is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the amount of the call or contribution` GREATER THAN (IF `the issue price of the share` MINUS (`the amount paid up on the share` PLUS `the amount reduced on the share`) GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the issue price of the share` MINUS (`the amount paid up on the share` PLUS `the amount reduced on the share`) ELSE 0)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member of the company (past or present) is not liable in respect of the issue price of any share to any call or contribution greater in amount than the difference (if any) between" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says a member is not liable above the difference; it does not say the member is liable up to it
